    "blocker": "From g(z)=f(z)·f(-z)≡0 on the disk, conclude f≡0. This requires the identity theorem: the zero set of a nonzero analytic function on a connected domain is discrete, so f·(f∘(-id))≡0 forces either f≡0 or f∘(-id)≡0, both giving f≡0. The identity theorem for analytic functions is available in Mathlib (IsolatedZeros) but connecting it to the product-zero implication needs care.",
